rk356x-yolov5n - Rockchip RK356x (RK3566/RK3568) NPU YOLOv5n demo for musl OpenWrt
================================================================================

Supported hardware
------------------
  Supported:     RK3566 / RK3568  (RK356x family, RKNPU1 NPU generation)
  NOT supported: RK3588 / RK3576  (different NPU generation, needs different
                                  .rknn models and a different librknnrt build)

What it installs
----------------
  /opt/yolov5/rknn_yolov5_demo             YOLOv5n demo (glibc ELF)
  /opt/yolov5/model/yolov5n_rk3566_i8.rknn YOLOv5n INT8 model (RK356x)
  /opt/yolov5/model/coco_80_labels_list.txt 80-class COCO label list
  /opt/yolov5/model/bus.jpg                sample image for a smoke test
  /opt/yolov5/run_yolov5n.sh               in-tree runner script
  /usr/bin/yolov5n                         wrapper script

Dependencies
------------
  This package does NOT ship its own glibc or RKNPU runtime; it depends on
  rk356x-npu-ocr, which provides:
      /opt/glibc/ld-linux-aarch64.so.1 + shared libraries
      /opt/rknpu/librknnrt.so
  That reuse saves 20 MB+ of duplicated payloads.

Usage
-----
  yolov5n /opt/yolov5/model/bus.jpg          single inference
  yolov5n /opt/yolov5/model/bus.jpg 100      loop 100x (FPS benchmark)

  The wrapper is equivalent to:
      cd /opt/yolov5
      /opt/glibc/ld-linux-aarch64.so.1 --library-path /opt/glibc:/opt/rknpu \
          ./rknn_yolov5_demo model/yolov5n_rk3566_i8.rknn <image> <loop_count>

  The demo resolves its label list relative to ./model/, hence the cd.

License notes
